    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date is rejected with HTTP 400, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (not Spring MVC).\n\n**Change in validation logic** \u2014 `ValidateOwner.java` (the single step that binds the `POST /api/owners` body):\n- Added a check that, when `registrationDate` is present and after `LocalDate.now()`, throws the new checked `OwnerRegistrationDateFutureException`. The check sits alongside the other field validations, before the body is republished for downstream steps.\n\n**New escalation (error \u2192 response) wiring**, mirroring the existing postcode/telephone handlers:\n- `OwnerRegistrationDateFutureException.java` \u2014 a checked exception carrying the submitted date.\n- `OwnerRegistrationDateFutureExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"registrationDate\"]}`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.OwnerRegistrationDateFutureException.yml` \u2014 maps the exception to the handler.\n\n**Tests:** The new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` (posts `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"`, expects 400) passes, and the full suite builds green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\nA note on scope: the existing `BusinessDay`/holiday roll-forward logic still applies to valid (non-future) dates; this change only adds the future-date rejection and doesn't touch that behavior.",
